                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h3]Easy RPG[/h3]\nAn easy single click type RPG, no hack and slash. No party management although you do get to choose a few helpers who come and go on their own depending on the plot. \n\n[i]Top-down view . [/i] Driftmoon is an interesting story with loads of often funny dialog, a lot of tricky puzzles, a lot of hidden bonus items to find and a bit of fighting in between.\n\n[h3]Simple RPG[/h3]\nYour character stats do matter, but not as much as you might think, you will want to choose between using a bow or the sword, but whichever you choose there is little penalty because you can pause the combat and cast buffs or swap weapons. Some monsters are best taken on with cold steel and others from afar. But there is no need for mental gymnastics, all very basic. What there is a lot of is dialog.\n\nThere is some crafting, for health potions and other items, but it's not like you spend a lot of time doing that. There are traders, and it will help to sell anything you do not want to them. Although I can give you one game clue, try to keep any items made of silver and of precious metals.\n\n[h3]Many Choices[/h3]\nIn between the humour are a lot of very real \"not-hero\" people whom you can choose to help or not to help. And these choices obviously affect the end game in different ways. The game is pretty dialog heavy and you might be inclined to skip a lot of it, and you can. Everything stays in the chat log, so you can scroll back, and things that matter sit in the quest log or in the scrolls you pick up with clues. I did find a few places where the next thing to do or item to locate was not entirely obvious. I could not find any text based guides sadly, it's a great game, but no guide. I did find lets-play videos which did help get past 2 tough spots.\n\n[h3]Collect fish and feathers and...[/h3]\nThis is not a game that really fits with the curated games, but it does feature Karma, every positive or negative choice you make gives you karma points, which are a party stats boost. Since it's pretty simple combat, and your choices are quite important I'm adding it and you can find it in this list : https://store.steampowered.com/curator/41773079-EmpathyGames/list/91358/",
